-- title:
--   Components through a supersingular point as Γ(ℓ)-translates
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), together with a prime $\ell$ satisfying $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the subgroup (`hH₁`) which is the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal (`hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of the congruence subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   Arithmetic base: $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, henselian local and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Further, $j \in K$ is a nonzero element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\prod\!$-normalised $j$-series transported to $L$ (`hj`); $\varpi \in A$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`); and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` denotes the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A K j` is $j$ regarded as an element of it; [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two localisation morphisms from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   Supersingular point data: $y$ is a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. A point $z$ of the two-chart model is given, together with the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism (`hϖz`), lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$ (`hz`); a point $y'$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}(\,$`chartAlgFin A K j`$)$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` (`hy'`), satisfying the same supersingularity condition `hss'` for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`).
--
--   Local Drinfeld chart data: $W_1$ is a discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with a ring homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ such that $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`); $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`, the congruence being against [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)); and $e_1$ is a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses, stated in terms of the stalk $\mathrm{STK}$ at $z$, its completion $\mathrm{CMP}$, the completion map $\mathrm{toC}$, the quotient $S$ with projection $\mathrm{mkS}$, and the canonical map $\mathrm{germY}$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\mathrm{STK}$ (composite of the inverse $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism, the inverse of the isomorphism on sections of `ιFin` over $\top$, and the germ at $z$ on the image open set). They assert: (i) for every $a \in A$, $e_1$ carries the completed germ of $a$ to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1 a))$; (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, the automorphism $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself; (iii) for every such $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ and every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra, the induced endomorphism of the chart algebra is the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, every `hpres`, and under the assumption that the induced endomorphism is the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the restriction of $\tau$, $\theta$ fixes the image of every constant $C(w)$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ for all $i,j$, moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ forces $c \equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$, while $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ together with $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$ forces $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$; (v) for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, each containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each admitting a linear witness $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h \in P_i$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $\mathrm{toC}$ followed by $e_1$ differ; (vi) for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and admitting such a linear witness with $(a,b) = (1,0)$, and for every $a$ in the chart algebra, $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient $\mathrm{coeff}_n(a)$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ in $L$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $q$-fold $q$-expansion rescaling of the $j$-series over $L$, lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and there exist $a_0 \in A$ with the corresponding chart element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that, first, for all $a,b \in W_1$ of which at least one is a unit and with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and second, $e_1$ sends $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY})$ of that difference to $\mathrm{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   Finally, let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a prime ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` (`h𝔭`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖ𝔭`), with $\mathfrak{p} \le y$ (`h𝔭y`) and $\mathfrak{p} \neq y$ (`h𝔭ne`).
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of $\delta \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\delta \in \Gamma(\ell)$ and $\delta \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and of an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ δ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero image over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image under `coeffEmb L` of the quotient of those series, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the product of $\iota$ applied coefficientwise to the Laurent series of $\tau x$ with the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta^{-1}$ — such that for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A K j`:
--   $$a \in \mathfrak{p} \iff \text{for every } n \in \mathbb{Z} \text{ there is } m \in \mathfrak{m}_A \text{ with } \mathrm{coeff}_n\bigl(\tau(a)\bigr) = \text{image of } m \text{ in } L.$$
--   Thus $\mathfrak{p}$ is the pullback along $\tau$ of the prime consisting of those chart elements all of whose Laurent coefficients are non-units of $A$.
--
--   This identifies every prime strictly below a supersingular maximal ideal of the $j$-finite chart algebra — equivalently, every component of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model through the chosen supersingular point — as the image, under a level automorphism attached to an element of $\Gamma(\ell) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, of the distinguished component cut out by the condition that all $q$-expansion coefficients be non-units; the version here is the auxiliary $H_1$-level frame, with $H_1$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo the guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$. It is used in the subsequent analysis of the supersingular points and components of the special fibre, including the Igusa-type computations and the valuation-subring descriptions of the components.
